# Build-context filter.
#
# Why this was the first file of the task: the built image is a separate
# observation channel that no git gate sees. Without this file the very first
# `docker build` would pack the private AI layer (`ai/`, 82 files) and 23M of
# `graphify-out/` into the image that ships to the customer.
#
# Ceiling, stated out loud: this file cuts the build context, not an already
# built image. Proof of absence is a check of the image contents
# (`docker export <c> | tar t | grep -cE '(^|/)ai/'` → 0), not this list.

# --- private AI layer (our IP) ---
ai/
.claude/
CLAUDE.md
README_ai.md
README_ai.md.*
setup/
graphify-out/
scripts/rule5-nudge.sh
# publication tooling — its patterns name the private layer; scripts/ is copied whole
scripts/private/
tests/private/

# --- secrets: never in the image ---
.env
.env.*
docker/

# --- local state and build artifacts (the image builds its own) ---
node_modules
.nuxt
.output
.git
.gitignore
.gitattributes
.nuxtrc
.playwright-mcp/
*.log

# --- tests: not needed at runtime (`test:ci` runs in CI, not in the image) ---
tests/
vitest.config.ts

# --- working-tree litter ---
/*.png
.DS_Store

# Warning: `scripts/` and `supabase/` are NOT excluded — they must be in the image.
# Ops without a host Node depends on them
# (`docker compose run --rm app node scripts/db-migrate.mjs`), i.e. a customer
# without sources applies migrations and seeds with the same application image.
